  "worked_solution": "First, we find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-(1)(-3) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +5+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4.$ Since we get two distinct eigenvalues, the matrix $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\nNow, we construct the diagonal matrix $D,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
